From 762c8ebea8be9ac69fbba78a7696922a89593385 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:19:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/56] Steering candidates: the sphere query's exact test
 after the cheap filters

CollectCollisionCandidates (FUN_005D3740, 0x005D3827..0x005D3A29) gathers
the units in a sphere around the mover through COGrid::ForAllEntitiesIterator
(0x00721FB0) - cell gather, then per entity an inner-box overlap or the
entity's own CollideSphere - and only then drops the ones it does not want:
non-units, source units (func_IsSourceUnit: itself, structures, other
layers...), units without steering, units on a PT_2 path.

Every test is a pure read, so the gathered entities now go through those
filters first and the sphere query's acceptance test only for the ones that
survive; the lists come out with the same units in the same grid order. The
acceptance test is COGrid::SphereQuery, which ForAllEntitiesIterator now uses
too (same test, and the same shared result block the binary threads through
the walk).

Verified with the 30-minute all-AI checksum run (identical over all 18002
beats).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8db55c60366dc64b2f50553b939da960f241d187)
